Default gem_module is GEM_module
This default module no longer uses StageIN and StageOUT.
To use a different module recreate the symbolic link to point to 
this module or use -module [path_to_module_name]

Documentation on script "create_maestro"

-----------------------
For those who have uploaded GEM via the SSM package:
Use create_maestro to create your suite.

Example:

create_maestro -location [mysuite_name] -cfg $gem_DIR/share/configurations/GEM_cfgs

(default configuration is $gem_DIR/share/configurations/GEM_cfgs)
(default module is $gem_DIR/share/gem-maestro/gem_module)

-----------------------

For those who have uploaded GEM via the GoaS method to use your own binaries,
scripts, etc.:

Here are 3 examples in creating maestro suites
a) create_maestro (uses GEM_cfgs configuration)
   creates maestro suite in
   $HOME/.suites/goas/$GEM_version/${gem_DIR}/GEM_cfgs_work-*
b) create_maestro -cfg configurations/GEM_cfgs_GY_FISL_H for example
   creates maestro suite in
   $HOME/.suites/goas/$GEM_version/${gem_DIR}/GEM_cfgs_GY_FISL_H_work-*
c) create_maestro -location TATA
   creates maestro suite using GEM_cfgs in
   $HOME/.suites/TATA

A link for each suite is made under ${gem_DIR}/work-*/suites/[name_of_suite]
for each maestro suite created.

Some extra notes/examples for "experiment.cfg"
GEM_version=GOAS:[full path to GIT clone work directory]:[GEM_version]:[compiler]
GEM_version=[5.3.0-a16] (for GEM version published in SSM)
GEM_ovbin=[full path to GEM binaries]
GEM_ovbin=release (to use binary in GEM version published in SSM)
GEM_settings=[full path]/gem_settings.nml
GEM_outcfg=[full path]/outcfg.out
GEM_ptopo=[1x1x1] (Npex Pes x Npey Pes x OMP_threads)
GEM_serverIO=[full path to MIMD.cfg file]
GEM_timing=1 (for timings using barriers, not recommended for OPS)
